# Playwright is a devDependency of a harness, not of the product. Installing it is one
# command (see README.md).
node_modules/

# THE LOCKFILE IS COMMITTED, and used to be ignored here.
#
# It was ignored on the reasoning that a harness's dependency tree does not need pinning —
# and that held right up until something other than a person had to install it. `npm ci` is
# the only install command that refuses to resolve anything not already written down, and it
# does not run at all without this file. Without it a CI runner installs whatever npm decides
# that morning, which is the same class of fact as "the deploy said success": true, and not
# an identity.
#
# It is 1 dependency and its two transitive packages. The cost of carrying it is a few
# hundred lines that change when someone bumps playwright on purpose.
!package-lock.json

# Screenshot evidence for ONE run. The tests are the artifact; these are the receipt, and a
# receipt that lands in git turns every UI tweak into a binary diff.
.shots/
